","question":"Which set is bounded?","options":["$\\{x\\in\\mathbb{Q}\\colon |x| \\le 3\\}$","$\\{x\\in\\mathbb{Q}\\colon |x| \\ge 3\\}$","$\\{x\\in\\mathbb{Q}\\colon x \\le 3\\}$","$\\{1/x\\colon x\\in\\mathbb{Q},\\ 0<x\\le 3\\}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"a2628a85b9801a3437d165f9","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_bounded_set_7359b04a_curated20261026_002","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Which $M$ shows that $[-2,5]$ is bounded using $[-M,M]$?","options":["$M = 5$","$M = 1$","$M = 2$","$M = 0$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"4494b40794aeca0434820e4c","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_bounded_set_7359b04a_curated20261026_003","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"All four listed real sets are bounded. Which one is not an interval under the convention on this page?","options":["$[-1,1]$","$(0,1)$","$\\{-2,0,3\\}$","$\\{0\\}=[0,0]$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"bb43642c3ee52723d303227b","time_limit":20},{"id":"expansion_006_bounded_set_curated20261026_004","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Given that $X\\subseteq\\mathbb{R}$ is bounded above, which additional property is necessary and sufficient for $X$ to be bounded?","options":["It is bounded below.","It is infinite.","It has a maximum.","It is nonempty."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"5d2d070a38b5d5e2e15bc05a","time_limit":20},{"id":"expansion_006_bounded_set_curated20261026_005","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"If $X$ is bounded and $Y\\subseteq X$, is $Y$ bounded?","options":["Yes; subsets inherit the bound","No; subsets can be unbounded","Only if $Y$ is finite or an interval","Yes, but only with a strictly smaller $M$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"49bcd69d43a23e8932996a38","time_limit":25},{"id":"expansion_006_bounded_set_curated20261026_006","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which quantified condition exactly expresses that $X\\subseteq\\mathbb{R}$ is unbounded?","options":["There exist $M>0$ and $x\\in X$ with $|x|>M$.","For every $M>0$ there exists $x\\in X$ with $|x|>M$.","For every $x\\in X$ there exists $M>0$ with $|x|\\le M$.","For every $M>0$, every $x\\in X$ satisfies $|x|>M$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"4e5d67f2d633f6a2208a08bf","time_limit":35},{"id":"expansion_006_bounded_set_curated20261026_007","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which quantities are guaranteed to exist for a nonempty bounded set of real numbers?","options":["both a supremum and an infimum","a maximum and a minimum","a supremum but possibly no infimum","a supremum lying in the set"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"cbaaa04937faceb55b4c203d","time_limit":20},{"id":"expansion_006_bounded_set_curated20261026_008","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $M,N>0$, $A\\subseteq[-M,M]$ and $B\\subseteq[-N,N]$. Which formula always provides a positive bound for $A\\cup B$ for every such choice?","options":["$\\max\\{M,N\\}$","$\\min\\{M,N\\}$","$(M+N)/2$","$MN$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"2f8ee61834ff013e52bf27ae","time_limit":30},{"id":"expansion_006_bounded_set_curated20261026_009","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which condition is equivalent to boundedness of a set $X\\subseteq\\mathbb{R}$?","options":["All elements lie within one finite distance of $0$.","Each element individually lies at a finite distance from $0$.","The set contains only finitely many elements.","The set is symmetric about $0$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9c55feb0a46435f2e8e251a6","time_limit":30}]}}